course: dictionary
lesson: 6700
title: October in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: October is a month name, and you can learn what it means by reading the words around it. The dictionary says October is the tenth month of the year. It has 31 days and comes after September and before November. «Halloween on 31 October grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival at the end of the harvest.» The date 31 October tells you it is a day in October.
explain: Clues can also tell you the season. «Halloween, 31 October 2026, is a Saturday, and Bonfire Night, 5 November, is 5 days later, on a Thursday.» Here October is linked to days of the week and to other dates, so you can check it on a calendar. Always ask: what does the sentence tell me about when this happened?
explain: Words from other places can mean different things in different seasons. In the UK and the USA, October is in autumn, which is called fall in America. In Australia and New Zealand, October comes in spring. So the same month can feel very different depending on where you live.
fact: October is the tenth month of the year.
fact: October has 31 days.
fact: October comes after September and before November.
fact: «October» is a noun, the name of a month, and it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Zhōngqiū jié», the Mid-Autumn or Moon Festival, falls in September or October, when families look at the full moon.
exercise: Which month comes after September? | August | *October | March | November
exercise: «Halloween on 31 October grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival.» Which month is Halloween in? | June | April | *October | January
exercise: Which month comes just before November? | September | December | *October | August
test: How many days does October have? | 29 | *31 | 28 | 30
test: Which month is the tenth month of the year? | *October | September | November | December
exam: In the UK, the clocks change on the last Sunday in «October», which is in which season? | *Autumn | Spring | Summer | Winter
